Understanding the workflow

PART 1️⃣ — SSH INTO EC2 (Windows → EC2)
1. Verify your .pem key location (ON YOUR WINDOWS PC)
Let’s assume your key is here (change if different):
C:\Users\Siris\Downloads\sla-dashboard-key.pem

If unsure, open File Explorer and confirm the filename.

2. Fix key permissions (VERY IMPORTANT on Windows)
Open PowerShell (not CMD) and run:
icacls "C:\Users\Siris\Downloads\sla-dashboard-key.pem" /inheritance:r
icacls "C:\Users\Siris\Downloads\sla-dashboard-key.pem" /grant:r "$($env:USERNAME):(R)"

This avoids the Permission denied (publickey) error.

3. SSH into EC2
Replace:


sla-dashboard-key.pem → your key name


3.89.119.181 → your EC2 public IPv4


ssh -i "C:\Users\Siris\Downloads\sla-dashboard-key.pem" ec2-user@3.89.119.181

When asked:
Are you sure you want to continue connecting?

Type:
yes

✅ You should now see:
[ec2-user@ip-xxx-xxx-xxx-xxx ~]$


PART 2️⃣ — CHECK STREAMLIT APP FILES (ON EC2)
4. Go to your home directory
cd ~
ls

You should see:
app.py
venv/

If you don’t see app.py, tell me before continuing.

5. Open app.py to verify content
nano app.py

Check:


API Gateway URL is correct


No syntax errors


To exit nano:
CTRL + X → Y → ENTER


PART 3️⃣ — ACTIVATE PYTHON ENVIRONMENT
6. Activate virtual environment
source venv/bin/activate

You should now see:
(venv) [ec2-user@ip-xxx ~]$


7. Verify Streamlit is installed
streamlit --version

If not found, install it:
pip install streamlit requests pandas plotly


PART 4️⃣ — RUN STREAMLIT APP (CORRECT WAY)
8. Run Streamlit (IMPORTANT FLAGS)
streamlit run app.py --server.address 0.0.0.0 --server.port 8501

Expected output:
You can now view your Streamlit app in your browser.

URL: http://0.0.0.0:8501

⚠️ 0.0.0.0 is correct — do NOT open it directly

PART 5️⃣ — OPEN PORT 8501 (SECURITY GROUP)
If the site doesn’t load, this is usually the issue.
9. Fix EC2 Security Group
AWS Console → EC2 → Instances → Your Instance
➡️ Security → Security groups → Edit inbound rules
Add:
TypeProtocolPortSourceCustom TCPTCP85010.0.0.0/0
Save rules ✅

PART 6️⃣ — OPEN DASHBOARD IN BROWSER
10. Open in your browser (ON YOUR LAPTOP)
http://3.89.119.181:8501

You should see SLA Freshness Dashboard

PART 7️⃣ — QUICK DEBUG COMMANDS (IF IT FAILS)
Check if Streamlit is running
ss -lntp | grep 8501

Check app logs
ps aux | grep streamlit

Kill old Streamlit process (if needed)
pkill -f streamlit

Then re-run step 8.
